ARCHITECTURE (mirrors the A7 TemperatureImpact / Geofences / RegenEfficiency precedents)
  ClimateControlPageModel.kt       framework-free: registration ids; parseClimateState (decodes the
                                   snake_case /climate/latest map + one /climate row → ClimateState, the web
                                   ClimateState with the frontend camelCase transform reproduced as a lenient
                                   snake_case decode); parseClimateHistory (web useClimateHistory ▸ safeArray);
                                   parseChargingFlags (web chargingLatest.not_enough_power_to_heat);
                                   ClimateDisplayPrefs (web useUnits) — convertTempFromSI at the boundary, the SI
                                   °C source never stored converted (Phase-48); comfortDisposition / comfortScore /
                                   comfortRating / tempDelta / deltaTarget / deltaStatus / keeperMode / heatOrdinal /
                                   coolOrdinal (web comfortBadge / heatStyle / keeperLabel); efficiencyStats (web
                                   efficiencyStats useMemo); chronoHistory + temperatureChartData + acFanChartData
                                   (web chronoHistory / convertedChartData); sortClimateHistory + climateHistoryColumnOf
                                   (web useSortToggle + climateAccessor); recordClimateControlPageOpened; mapData; clockLabel.
  ClimateControlPageIcons.kt       locally-authored stroked 24×24 glyphs (Thermometer, ThermometerSun, Wind, Sun,
                                   Power, Flame, Settings, RefreshCw, Activity, Monitor); Snowflake / BatteryCharging /
                                   AlertTriangle / Bolt→Zap / Gauge→CircleGauge / Shield→ShieldCheck re-exported from
                                   DataDisplayGlyphs (the TemperatureImpactPageIcons precedent — shared catalogs unedited).
  ClimateControlPageSource.kt      seam over container.api (GET /climate/latest, /climate, /charging-telemetry/latest —
                                   each ?vehicle_id via the shared resilient safeRequest, folded to a loading→success/error
                                   Resource stream, the TemperatureImpactPageSource precedent, since the web issues these
                                   reads via query hooks with no domain store) + SelectedVehicleStore (web useSelectedVehicle)
                                   + SettingsStore.settings (web useUnits). No HTTP in the view.
  ClimateControlPageViewModel.kt   BaseFeedViewModel; climateState: StateFlow<UiState<ClimateState>> (web useClimate, empty
                                   when blank / no vehicle); historyState: StateFlow<UiState<List<ClimateState>>> (web
                                   useClimateHistory); chargingFlags: StateFlow<ChargingTelemetryFlags> (web
                                   useChargingTelemetryLatest, last-known); displayPrefs StateFlow (web useUnits);
                                   refresh / retry / recordViewOpened. No HTTP in the view.
  ClimateControlPageHost.kt        ClimateControlRoute reads LocalDataContainer, builds the source via
                                   climateControlPageSourceOf, binds ClimateControlPage; ClimateControlPageHost.register()
                                   wires the `climateControl` destination (Destinations.kt L103 page("climateControl",
                                   "/climate-control", NavGroup.VehicleSystems)). Registered once at process start by
                                   TeslaSyncApplication (idempotent).
  ClimateControlPage.kt            stateful entry (constructs the VM, records view.opened, collects the 3 feeds +
                                   displayPrefs) + stateless ClimateControlPageContent — the 36 panels, the 3 RadialGauges,
                                   the temperature LineChart, the AC/fan area+line ComboChart, and the sortable history
                                   DataTable; SI→display conversion only here via ClimateDisplayPrefs; no region is hidden.

NAV BOOT
  TeslaSyncApplication imports io.teslasync.android.vehiclesystems.climatecontrol.ClimateControlPageHost and calls
  ClimateControlPageHost.register() alongside the other A7 hosts (after TemperatureImpactPageHost.register()).

LIVE / STALENESS
  None of the three reads is an SSE live source (the web page polls via TanStack Query refetchInterval, not /events),
  so no >2-min staleness chip is rendered — the web page renders none either. ADR-013 freshness is preserved through
  the UiState the VM exposes.

