STRING CATALOG
  96 translation_climate_* keys were added to res/values/strings.xml, res/values-ar/strings.xml and
  res/values-he/strings.xml (English values verbatim from the web i18n defaults so the per-language MissingTranslation
  lint stays clean — the ar/he catalogs are the English-seeded parity scaffold, mirroring the existing translation_regen_*
  rows). 84 of these are the manifest's required parity strings (enumerated above); the remaining 12 carry the page's
  dynamically-keyed literals that the manifest extractor cannot statically see — the five seat-position labels
  (Front Left/Right, Rear Left/Center/Right), the three heat-level labels (Low/Medium/High), the two comfort-badge
  labels (Adjusting, Far from target), and the two climate-keeper modes (Dog Mode, Camp Mode) — so the page has ZERO
  hardcoded visible literals. No `&` unescaped (AC State &amp; Fan Speed); no positional-format strings → no
  StringFormatInvalid. A case-sensitive scan confirms no duplicate resource names in any of the three catalogs.

ANONYMOUS REGIONS REPRODUCED (beyond the named panels)
  - The page chrome title + muted subtitle (web PageContainer title=Climate Control / subtitle="HVAC status, …").
  - The web `actions={<VehicleSelect /> + Refresh}` — the shared sharedsurfaces VehicleSelect(withIcon) + a Ghost
    Refresh Button (RefreshCw) wired to viewModel.refresh().
  - The HVAC banner trailing chips (keeper / defrost(mode) / battery-heater / insufficient-power), each condition-gated.
  - The three thermal-comfort rings (score / signed delta / warm-cold-comfortable status glyph), each tinted by its band.
  - The seat-grid auto-climate chips, the seat-cooling ventilation badge, and the 0–3 heat-level legend strip.
  - Both history charts' accessible data-table fallbacks (ChartContainer dataTableHeader/Rows) for the opaque canvases.
  - The `Climate Control` document title (web usePageTitle) exposed as the scroll container's accessible name (semantics).

